# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unity — 3D Pull-The-World
# Based on github/gitignore/Unity.gitignore, with project-specific additions.
# Root-anchored (leading /) wherever a same-named folder could legitimately
# exist inside Assets/, so we never ignore real project content by accident.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Unity-generated caches and build intermediates
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emory[Cc]aptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/
/[Aa]rtifacts/
/[Cc]odeCoverage/
/.utmp/
/ExportedObj/
/[Aa]ssets/[Ss]treamingAssets/aa*

# Asset meta files must be kept for everything we DO commit
!/[Aa]ssets/**/*.meta

# Auto-generated VS / Rider / MSBuild project files (Unity regenerates these)
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db
*.tmp
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# IDE / editor local state
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
.gradle/
.consulo/
**/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
RiderScriptEditorPersistedState.asset

# Claude Code local (machine-specific) settings — shared settings.json is tracked
.claude/settings.local.json

# Node — the MCP bridge server's dependencies and compiled output are
# reinstallable via `npm ci && npm run build` inside Packages/mcp-unity/Server~
node_modules/
/[Pp]ackages/mcp-unity/Server~/build/
/[Pp]ackages/mcp-unity/Server~/log.txt
/[Pp]ackages/mcp-unity/Server~/log.txt.meta

# Test + capture output (regenerated by the PlayMode test run — see README)
/[Cc]aptures/
results.xml
*.TestResults.xml
# The Test Runner writes a temporary bootstrap scene into Assets/ for the duration of a PlayMode
# run and normally deletes it afterwards. It survives an interrupted run, and it is worthless.
/[Aa]ssets/InitTestScene*.unity
/[Aa]ssets/InitTestScene*.unity.meta

# PicReference/ is deliberately TRACKED as of the v2 rework.
#
# The v1 README said to exclude it on git init, on the grounds that it was concept art from a
# parallel session that the build did not use. That stopped being true: PALETTE.md and
# VISUAL_LANGUAGE.md in there are now the working art direction for the game, and the panel
# renders are what the capture-compare loop judges against. Reference material that decides what
# the game looks like belongs in the repo. It is ~11 MB of PNG, which is a rounding error next to
# the 7 GB of Library/ this file already excludes.

# Builds / packages / crash reports
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app
*.ipa
/[Bb]uild[Rr]eports/
build-output.properties
crashlytics-build.properties
sysinfo.txt

# Credential-bearing files (must never be committed)
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/GoogleService-Info*.plist*
**/google-services*.json*
secrets.json

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.orig
*.orig.meta

# Showcase renders: frame sequences and intermediates are rebuilt from the Unity tests + ffmpeg
/PullTheWorld_Showcase/RawCaptures/
